.TH DUSK 1 "2026-11-06" "dusk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dusk \- a logout and power menu for Hyprland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dusk
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dusk check
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B dusk preview
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B dusk doctor
.br
.B dusk init
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dusk
opens one fullscreen layer-surface menu on the focused monitor and a dim-only surface on every
other monitor. Choosing an action runs it and exits; pressing the keybind again closes a running
menu. No background daemon is left behind.
.PP
With no config file dusk uses the built-in
.B dusk
theme. The config lives at
.I ~/.config/dusk/config.kdl
(or
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dusk/config.kdl ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dusk
Open the menu, or close it if it is already open. A second launch signals the first instance over
a Unix socket under
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.TP
.BI "dusk check [" path ]
Parse the config and every action override, reporting file and line numbers. Exits non-zero when
there is a problem; the menu would still open with the settings that parsed.
.TP
.BI "dusk preview [" path ]
Open the real menu with live reload. Saving the config swaps the look and tokens. Actions only
print.
.TP
.B dusk doctor
Report the session, compositor, layer-shell, Hyprland blur rule, locker, notification tool and
logind capabilities and inhibitors.
.TP
.B dusk init
Write a commented starter config, if none exists, and print the Hyprland blur rule.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
Use
.I PATH
instead of the default config.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Open the real menu, but actions only print. This is the safe way to try a config.
.TP
.B \-\-force
With
.B init
, overwrite an existing config.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
Rune's headless flags pass through:
.BR \-\-snap " FILE, " \-\-scene " NAME, " \-\-tree " FILE, " \-\-script " FILE, "
.BR \-\-frames " N, " \-\-at " SECONDS, " \-\-size " WxH, " \-\-theme " light|dark."
.SH CONFIGURATION
A config is KDL and is merged over the theme:
.PP
.nf
theme "dusk"
layout "row"
appearance "auto"
tokens { accent "#d38be0"; radius 28 }
tokens "light" { dim "white/40" }
hide "hibernate"
order "lock" "logout" "suspend" "reboot" "shutdown"
action "logout" { run "hyprshutdown"; key "e" }
action "firmware" {
    label "Firmware"
    icon "~/.config/dusk/icons/chip.svg"
    run "systemctl reboot --firmware-setup"
    key "f"
    confirm #true
}
.fi
.PP
Themes are looks only: they may set
.BR extends ", " layout " and " tokens .
An action, hide/order or appearance setting in a theme is reported and ignored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dusk/config.kdl
The config.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dusk/themes/*.kdl
Themes by id.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dusk.lock
Single-instance lock.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dusk.sock
Toggle socket.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, closed, or toggled another instance.
.TP
.B 1
.B check
found problems.
.TP
.B 3
No display, event loop, layer-shell surface or renderer.
.TP
.B 70
The watchdog found the menu unresponsive and removed it.
.SH SAFETY
Shutdown, reboot and log out need a second press within three seconds. Key repeat, held launch
keys and a second press within 250 ms never count. Lock and suspend fire at once, unless the action
sets
.BR confirm " #true."
Built-ins appear only when logind returns
.B yes
or
.BR challenge ;
an inhibitor keeps the menu open and names the blocker. All surfaces are destroyed before a
command is spawned. Automated tests and development should use
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.B preview
or a headless run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hyprctl (1),
.BR loginctl (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1)
